speechtext:
That a sum not exceeding $20,003,428,213.05 being the aggregate of:
(a)	nine-twelfths of the total amounts of the items set forth in the Estimates for the year ending March 31, 1981, laid before the House of Commons on April 22, 1980, with the exception of Social Development Vote I, $18,701,054,379.72;
(b)	an additional three-twelfths of the total amounts of Energy, Mines and Resources Vote L35, External Affairs Votes L35, L40 and L45, Regional Economic Expansion Vote 30, Transport Vote 35 and Treasury Board Vote 10 (Schedule A) of the said Estimates, $77,607,000.00;
(c)	an additional two-twelfths of the total amounts of Agriculture Vote 10, Employment and Immigration Vote 30, Energy, Mines and Resources Votes 1 and 15, External Affairs Vote 15, Finance Vote 5, Indian Affairs and
Supply
Northern Development Votes 15, 30, L35 and L40, Industry, Trade and Commerce Votes 10, L30 and L40, Justice Vote 5, Labour Vote 5, Public Works Vote 35, Secretary of State Votes 20, 55, 80 and 105, Transport Vote L95 and Treasury Board Vote 5 (Schedule B) of the said Estimates, $675,361,325.00;
(d)	an additional one-twelfth of the total amounts of Communications Vote 10, Employment and Immigration Votes 15 and 20, Energy, Mines and Resources Vote L80, Environment Vote 30, External Affairs Vote 25, Indian Affairs and Northern Development Votes 20, 45 and L50, National Defence Votes 1 and 5, National Health and Welfare Vote 10, Privy Council Votes I and 20, Public Works Vote 30, Secretary of State Votes 15, 30, 50, 65 and 85, Supply and Services Vote 1 and Veterans Affairs Vote 25 (Schedule C) of the said Estimates, $549,405,508.33;
be granted to Her Majesty on account of the fiscal year ending March 31, 1981.
